  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the quai de l'Amiral Courbet, by the small harbour of Villefranche-sur-Mer, Achill's brings together three spaces: a dining room with a waterfront terrace, a bar area and a rooftop overlooking the bay. The Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office counts 120 covers, all on the terrace. It is a family business: the website explains that it opened in 1975 as the Calypso, then was taken over and renamed Achill's in 2010 by the founder's grandchildren.</p>
      <p>The menu, described on the website as multicultural and rich in fresh produce, comes with a board of daily specials featuring wild fish brought in by local fishermen. The rooftop is dedicated to cocktails, with a finger-food menu for after work; the website says the roof is open in summer.</p>
      <h2>Opening hours and booking</h2>
      <p>The official website announces opening 7 days a week from 9am to 1:30am, with the rooftop from 6pm to 1:30am Tuesday to Friday. The restaurant's Instagram account gives other hours (restaurant 12pm to 11pm, rooftop 6:30pm to 1am): hours probably vary with the season, so a call before you come clears up any doubt. Bookings on 06 17 44 10 28; tables of more than 10 people are accepted on request.</p>
      <h2>Good to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Neither the restaurant's website nor the tourist office page says whether dogs are allowed: the tourist office answers "not communicated, please contact the establishment". Only a commercial directory (PagesJaunes, repeated by Mappy) lists "animals accepted", with no conditions. With your dog, call before you come to find out whether it can sit with you on the terrace, and when it is least busy.</p>
      <p>As for the address, the official website gives 2 quai de l'Amiral Courbet and the tourist office number 1: it is the same quay, by the harbour, and the restaurant is easy to spot.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the quay is a busy thoroughfare, especially on cruise-ship days; with a dog, aim for a quiet time and bring water.</div>
    </div>
